                    "description": "The core motif of PasA precursor peptide is ether cross-linked by PasB followed by proteolysis. The cleaved ether cross-linked hexapeptide (QWTFRF) is acetylated at N-terminal of Gln by PasC to produce mature aphotorhaptin A (Ac-QWTFRF). Aphotorhaptin A is a photorhaptin analog distinguished by an additional N-acetylated Gln residue at its N-terminus. PasC also exhibits remarkable substrate promiscuity towards diverse acyl-CoA donors and peptide substrates."
